From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:45:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fixup! logging: write log lines on a logger thread

Add an explicit logger-aware fork lifecycle at the daemon and LockDirectory test fork sites. With application logging producers/configuration quiescent, no live EventBuilder and child-compatible sinks/callbacks, stop/join/drain the logger before fork and restart independently in parent and child, including the parent on fork failure. Preserve fork errno. No hot-path changes, child error suppression or arbitrary concurrent-fork safety claim.

The bounded native regression covers repeated parent/child cycles, child warnings and errors, explicit flush, continued parent logging and exactly-once queued-parent delivery. It deliberately uses only APIs already present at this original async owner; typed Error and FinishLogging controls belong to the later-context integration probe, not this prefix test.

Before: unmodified focused util_tests/test_LockDirectory timed out at8 seconds. Artifact real logger probe after: full-ring child backlog131072 actually written, WARN/plain+typed ERROR and full-ring WARN/ERROR delivered,zero drops; parent queued once and continues; injected EAGAIN preserves errno and restarts parent; pre-start fork preserves buffering/no thread. Actual source/native/full checks are recorded separately and never inferred from replay.

Manually authored lifecycle correction, not a scripted call conversion. Original owner-context transport excludes State snapshot, precision, conversion tail and later typed/shutdown APIs.
